## Lore

Hunters fly beside the Hounds as the aerial scouts, messengers and assassins of
the Nightlords. Like the Hounds they wear black skeletal armor that is really
their own body, but their helmet-heads carry a long curved vulture''s beak and
two bat-like wings rise from their backs. An army typically fields one Hunter
for every ten Hounds, and they share the Hounds'' appetite for hunting down and
killing the innocent.

In the Nightlands, patrols of 4D4 Hunters fly the roads between the city-states
and the borders of their master''s domain, watching for intruders, enemy armies
and monsters out of the Waste. They were used heavily in the early invasion of
Earth, especially for assassinations, and are at their most dangerous against
victims in high-rise buildings. Their occasional patrols over Earth cities have
produced a crop of monster sightings that the Nightlord-controlled authorities
ignore.

## GM Notes

Alliances and allies: Hunters work alongside the Hounds and the other minions of
the Nightlords.

Average life span is unknown; they may live for centuries but are usually
killed in combat or war. As NPCs they start at 1D4+2 level, and almost none
progress beyond 6th.

Weapons: Darkblade Scimitars (2D6 plus base P.S. damage). They are rarely issued
anything else, though a few wield Darkblade Spears (3D6 plus base P.S. damage).
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nb-hunter');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
